@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Common questions"; }
<section class="pub-page-top container"><p class="pub-kicker">COMMON QUESTIONS</p><h1>A few answers.<br /><em>A clearer start.</em></h1><p class="pub-lead">Find out how exam entry, monitoring, saved answers and results work.</p><label class="pub-search" for="faqSearch"><i class="bi bi-search" aria-hidden="true"></i><input id="faqSearch" type="search" aria-label="Search common questions" placeholder="Search a question, e.g. camera or results" autocomplete="off" /></label><p id="faqCount" class="pub-small" role="status" aria-live="polite">16 questions</p></section><section class="container pub-faq-layout"><nav class="pub-faq-nav" aria-label="Question topics"><a href="#getting-started">Getting started</a><a href="#monitoring">Monitoring</a><a href="#answers-and-results">Answers and results</a><a href="#help">Help</a></nav><div><section class="pub-faq-group" id="getting-started"><h2>Getting started</h2><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Who can register?</summary><p>Students and teachers can create accounts. Teacher access requires administrator approval. Exam access also depends on assignment, eligibility and the scheduled entry window.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Why can I not see my exam?</summary><p>Check your account, the exam date and start time. Ask your teacher to confirm your assignment or eligibility. An exam may not be open for entry yet.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>What do I need before starting?</summary><p>Keep your device charged and use a stable connection. Complete identity and device checks, and allow the permissions required by your exam.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Why do I need identity photos?</summary><p>Your registration and examination identity checks help confirm that the registered candidate is taking the test. Follow the photo instructions on screen and use a clear, well-lit camera view.</p></details></section><section class="pub-faq-group" id="monitoring"><h2>Monitoring</h2><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Will I be asked to share my screen?</summary><p>If the examination requires screen monitoring, the browser will ask you to choose what to share. The website cannot silently grant permission. Select the entire display when the setup instructions require it.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Does a monitoring alert mean I have been found cheating?</summary><p>An observation alone is not a final finding. Confirmed qualifying events can add warnings or pause the exam under the teacher’s settings. Teachers can review the available evidence and circumstances.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>When can an examination be blocked?</summary><p>The teacher sets the qualifying categories and warning limit. When automatic blocking is enabled, the next qualifying event after the allowed warnings can pause the attempt. Protective identity holds and technical holds have separate recovery requirements.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>What if I leave fullscreen or switch tabs?</summary><p>Follow the examination rules and remain on the exam page. Supported browser events may be recorded and may qualify for warnings. Exiting fullscreen and stopping screen sharing are different actions.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Can the website see every tab or another device?</summary><p>A normal website cannot list all hidden tabs or control another physical device. An authorised shared display shows what is visible on that display; it does not provide complete browser history.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Who can review my recordings?</summary><p>Evidence access is restricted by the system’s account roles and examination permissions. Ask your organiser about the applicable recording and retention rules before the examination.</p></details></section><section class="pub-faq-group" id="answers-and-results"><h2>Answers and results</h2><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Are my answers saved automatically?</summary><p>The exam saves answers as you work. Check the saving status on screen. If saving fails, follow the message and contact your teacher; do not assume an unsaved answer reached the server.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>What happens if my connection drops?</summary><p>Read any recovery message and tell your teacher if the problem continues. Saved answers can be recovered through the authorised workflow, but an interrupted connection may affect timing and monitoring. Avoid opening duplicate exam tabs.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>How do I finish a session?</summary><p>Review your answers and choose Submit session. Wait for confirmation. If the examination has more sessions, follow the break or continuation instructions.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>Why is my result not available yet?</summary><p>Your attempt may be awaiting processing, teacher review or release. Check My Results and contact your teacher if the expected publication time has passed.</p></details></section><section class="pub-faq-group" id="help"><h2>Help</h2><details class="pub-faq"><summary>What should I do if the camera or microphone stops?</summary><p>Follow the device-recovery message. Check that the device is connected and browser permission is allowed. A technical issue is not by itself proof of physical absence or misconduct. Contact your teacher if recovery does not work.</p></details><details class="pub-faq"><summary>What information should I send when asking for help?</summary><p>Include your Candidate ID, exam name, the time of the problem and the exact message shown. Share an error screenshot only with your authorised teacher or support team, and never send your password.</p></details></section><p id="faqEmpty" hidden>No questions match that search. Try a shorter word or <a href="/Home/Contact">open the help guide</a>.</p></div></section><section class="container pub-help-bar"><div><h2>Still need a hand?</h2><p>Start with the practical troubleshooting guide.</p></div><a class="pub-button" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Contact">Get help →</a></section>
